Package: radiator-yubikey
Architecture: all
Depends: perl, sqlite3 | postgresql-client, python3 (>= 3.11), ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: libcrypt-rijndael-perl
Suggests: libauth-yubikey-decrypter-perl, libdbd-sqlite3-perl, libdbd-pg-perl,
          openssl, frr
Description: YubiKey OTP database tools for Radiator RADIUS
 Scripts that create and manage the SQLite or PostgreSQL database of users
 and YubiKeys that Radiator's <AuthBy SQLYUBIKEY> checks one-time passwords
 against, with no dependency on Yubico's cloud: add, import, verify, back up
 and restore accounts, move from SQLite to PostgreSQL, keep logging users in
 at a site that is cut off (partition mode), advertise an anycast
 address only while Radiator accepts logins, and set up three sites from
 one input file (yubikey-turnkey).
 .
 Installed in /opt/radiator-yubikey. Radiator, from Radiator Software's
 packages or its source, is not a dependency, so either works;
 /opt/radiator-yubikey/install.sh checks for it and installs the Perl
 modules and database tools it needs.
